marry here with a news update  CD Projekt RED once again flies in the  face of major publishers announcing  today that anyone who purchases The  Witcher 3 will get 16 DLC packs for free  the first pack will be released the day  after the game comes out on February  24th it contains an armor set as well as  new hairstyles for Geralt  nice beard 2 DLC bundles will be  released weekly after that until all 16  packs are released including alternative  looks for other main characters such as  yennefer as well as new quests the  reasoning behind giving out all the DLC  for free was given by the CD Projekt RED  co-founder in an open letter to fans as  gamers we nowadays have to hold on tight  to our wallet as surprisingly right  after release lots of tiny pieces of  tempting content materialized with a  steep price tag attached haven't we just  paid a lot of cash for a brand new game  as CD Projekt RED we strongly believe  this is not the way it should work and  with The Witcher 3 Wild Hunt we have  decided to do it differently this is our  way of saying thank you for buying our  game he goes on to say that this is not  a pre-order bonus you get the DLC if you  buy before or after the release date  it's also not limited to the collector's  edition or physical copies every copy of  the game gets you a free ride on the DLC  train choo-choos not that we need any  more reasons to anticipate The Witcher 3  pretty sure we're all excited about it  for more gaming news  I recommend gamespot.com slash news  nice beard
 

